A||N||2||FieroSTETZ||is there any way to use a multiband o2||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||02-06-2001||12:15 PM||||is there any way to use a multiband o2 sensor on a fiero? when my laptop is hooked up, the thing only says "rich" or "lean" (1,0) would a multiband work with the fiero ecm, or would i have to add that additionally, and have to use an AFR gauge?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||02-06-2001||07:11 PM||||There is nothing wrong with the present system. It's doing exactly what it should. The ECM only reports R/L not how far R or L. This is an ECM programming issue not an O2 sensor issue.<P>If you are doing performance work you will have to add a A/F meter to get more resolution from the sensor or simply learn how to use a DVM.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-06-2001||07:42 PM||||ogre is right.. Autometer, VDO, PMS, and Haltech all make readable air/fuel meters. for more accuracy get a 3 wire heated O2 and install that.. but at $70 a pop the stock OS101 from NAPA ($19) is good enough for most light shows in the car. ||||reg||1
